

POLHEMUS INSTALL
======================================

https://github.com/ana-GT/trackerd

1) Get fxload

    # apt-get install fxload

2) Get libusb-1.0

    # apt-get install libusb-1.0-0-dev
    
    or manually
    
    $ wget ftp://ftp.polhemus.com/pub/Linux_tools/libusb-1.0.0.tar.bz2
    $ tar -xjf libusb-1.0.0.tar.bz2
    $ cd libusb-1.0.0
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    # make install

3) Install Linux Driver for Polhemus (piterm)

    $ wget ftp://ftp.polhemus.com/pub/Linux_tools/piterm-1.0.4.tar.gz
    $ tar -xzf piterm-1.0.4.tar.gz
    $ cd piterm-1.0.4
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    # make install
  
    $ ls /usr/local/share/PolhemusUsb/

4) Instal rules file

    $ cd piterm-1.0.4/fw.rules/
    # cp 90-Polhemus_trkr.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/

5) Reload rules.d

   $ su root
   # udevadm control --reload-rules
   # mount --bind /dev/bus /proc/bus
   # ln -s /sys/kernel/debug/usb/devices /proc/bus/usb/devices

6) Eventually reboot OS


POLHEMUS START
==============

1) Power on the Liberty station
2) The light indicator on the foreface must enlight with green color
   * If is enlights with red color ou blinks with red color, then put sensors closer to the source
3) Plug in the USB cable






